es grade eight a system  is set up to make it easy to get to the  right high school with minimum fuss but  the same cannot be said for the  transition between secondary and  post-secondary education right  historically most individuals finish  their education at the end of high  school and college and university was  intended for a relative few but since  then the demand for those with  post-secondary credentials has massively  increased but the process to get there  has remained basically as always been  students still have to figure out where  they want to go they have to find the  application we have to pay a fee and  then they have to figure out how they're  going to afford to go and so if the  process to go to keep going we're going  to have to do we're going to think more  about it so I suggest you in short the  reason why some individuals not all but  some don't go on  to post sancta secondary there's two  reasons one the process not simple and  is not salient and two there's not  enough help to deal with the process and  so if we can't simplify things more  we're going to have to perhaps offer  some help so here's an example this is  the FAFSA the Free Application for  Federal Student Aid every individual in  the US they want to qualify for  financial aid to go to college or just  learn about their eligibility they have  to fill out this form the paper form of  the FAFSA is 10 pages with more than a  hundred questions very personalized  information and specific information  things like exact earnings exact income  Social Security numbers and a signature  at the end to say that all of this is  correct if not maybe I might have to go  to jail or face a fine of twenty  thousand dollars and so if the process  of the FAFSA can't be simplified further  or if individuals are just not accessing  the form maybe a helping hand could help  what I have in mind is something that I  call personal assistants personal  assistants is one on one help from  someone experienced ideally someone you  trust and who genuinely cares about your  well-being it's a kind of hand-holding  at an opportune time it's someone coming  up to saying look I know you're probably  already interested in this but just  haven't don't know where to get started  don't know how to go about it or haven't  figured out how to change your routine  or get around round to it I have  experience with this I want to help you  and why don't we just sit down get it  right done right now there's lots of  opportunities for personal assistance to  a friend or a son or daughter  from a policy perspective is a little  bit more tricky because you have to come  up with situations with this  face-to-face contact with trusted agents  on a large scale so the idea my  colleagues in high had to help with the  FAFSA is to partner with a tax  preparation company in the US the taxes  are completed around the same time that  the FAFSA has to be completed and a lot  of the information on the FAFSA is the  same information contained on the tax  form and so if you could pre populate  the FAFSA with the information from the  tax form there'd only be a few remaining  questions that you would have to walk  through so we teamed up with art H&amp;R  block which is you may know is a large  tax preparation company that fills out  forms mostly for low-income families the  company actually filled out more than 20  million forms last year and in our  experiment a parent would come in to get  their taxes done at H&amp;R Block who has a  child in grade 12 transitioning out of  high school and they were asked at  random by the same person who just spent  an hour with them on their taxes whether  they wanted to stick around for an extra  10 minutes to get the FAFSA done for the  son or daughter so how can this help  there's actually a lot of ways that  personal assistance might be working one  is that it gets the thing that you're  trying to get them to do it makes it  more visible more salient just bringing  up the FAFSA might be enough to remind  the individual that they were intending  to do this or that this is something  they want to do personal assistance is  also it reduces complexity it removes  the need to go through the instructions  or go through the think about the forms  or worry about making mistakes when  you're filling out the form in fact in  our study the participants deavon didn't  even have to look at the form they just  had to respond to questions being asked  by the tax professional  and personal assistance can be  convenient if it's offered at an  opportune time it's a lot easier to sit  down with someone when you're already at  their office then to ask them to work  through on their own find time to carve  out change the routine and get it done  on their own and it can be reassuring  you have someone who is trying to help  you and is encouraging to get this form  done you're more likely to think that  it's a good idea and finally involves  social interaction you're working with  someone if you have any questions or  concerns you can get immediate feedback  it's a lot easier to change your routine  when someone's right there holding your  hand through it then leaving it up to  someone on their own to watch a video on  the internet or to read something so  let's see what happened in the  comparison group that didn't receive any  help in completing the FAFSA the filing  rates for about forty percent remember  these students were transitioning out of  high school so it's not surprising that  there were at least some filing but in  the in the personal assistance group the  filing rates went up to fifty six  percent a 16 percentage point difference  so that's a big change it didn't go up  to a hundred percent because the  students still have to sign the FAFSA  and they're not in the office so the  best we can do was complete the form and  then we sent it home first for the  parent to get the student to sign and  then put in a prepaid envelope and send  it back still things get interesting now  when looking later to see who's in  college a year later and the comparison  group thirty percent are in college in  the personal assistance group it goes up  to forty percent a ten percentage point  increase so think about that for a  moment we made the difference between  not going and going to college for one  in every ten people in our sample at  one-third increase that's big and not  only did did we get them to go but we  got them to stay the results for going  for two consecutive  years are about the same and as striking  as these results are we think we can do  better there was that issue with the  signature and also we only help with the  financial aid form we didn't do anything  about the second form that needs  completing which is the program  application and we were only able to  help families i went to H&amp;R Block so why  not go directly to the high schools  especially the ones that are low  transition the ones were safe fewer than  half of them are going on and that's the  motivation behind the life after high  school project which is going on right  now here in Ontario across low  transition high schools throughout the  province and is sponsored by the  Ministry of training colleges in India  and universities and the idea is the  same we try to simplify the process and  follow up with personal assistance in  class so that every grade 12 student  leaving a high school does so with an  offer of acceptance with the program  that they help choose and a financial  aid package so that the bridge from high  school to post-secondary starts to look  like the bridge from Grade seven to  eight it's still the students choice on  whether they want to cross that bridge  but at least the option value becomes  more real so this is going on now there  the workshops are being done in class  and the applications are being paid for  by us and we'll see what happens maybe  in a year from now I'll be giving them  to talk about that so I want to conclude  by noting that having to fill out a form  is an easy example of where personalized  assistance and simplification can help  and college applications are just one  example we can also think of things like  helping students take the right courses  so they stay on an academic track or  that they graduate on time we're helping  parents with the form for the registered  education savings  but you can also think about personal  assistants more than just helping with  forums but as a general way to encourage  better behavior you can think of it as a  way for example of setting up a routine  and making easier to take tutorials to  attend tutorials in life there are lots  of situations not just in education  where we tend to follow routine and we  tend to take the path of least  resistance and when you have that  perspective you realize that there's a  lot of opportunity for personal  assistance not just an education and so  I hope you'll think about these and  maybe come up with your own ways to help  others and help yourselves thanks  you
 

